slam node periodically takes snapshots of laser scan (/scan) and odometry data (/odometry) and stores it internally

to run the node:
ros2 run slam slammer

to request the slam data (ROS2)

    - send std_msgs::msg::Bool true to /slam/cloud/request_data
    - it will respond with a JointState in global coordinates on /slam/cloud/xyz

    - jointstate data:
        - these are all float64 arrays
        - position: x data
        - velocity: y data
        -   effort: z data

    - it tries to filter out invalid points (inf, nan)
